where n is the number of moles of each gas.

First, we need the standard molar entropies (S°) of CO, CO₂, and O₂ at 298 K. These values can be found in standard tables:

- S°(CO) = 170.9 J/mol·K
- S°(CO₂) = 213.7 J/mol·K
- S°(O₂) = 205.2 J/mol·K

The balanced reaction is:

CO(g) + 1/2 O₂(g) → CO₂(g)

