1. **Determine the possible truth values for P, Q, and R:**  
   Since there are three statements, there are \( 2^3 = 8 \) possible combinations of train values for \( P \), \( Q \), and \( R \).

2. **Compute the truth values of \( P \rightarrow Q \), \( Q \rightarrow R \), and \( P \rightarrow R \) for each combination:**  
   - \( P \rightarrow Q \) is only false when \( P \) is true and \( Q \) is false.
   - \( Q \rightarrow R \) is only false when \( Q \) is true and \( R \) is false.
   - \( P \rightarrow R \) is only false when \( P \) is true and \( R \) is false.

3. **Compute the truth value of the antecedent \( (P \rightarrow Q) \wedge (Q \rightarrow R) \):**
   This is the conditional condition (statement) is only false when both statements \( P \rightarrow Q \) and \( Q \rightarrow R \) are false.

4. **Compute the truth value of the entire statement \( (P \rightarrow Q) \wedge (Q \to R) \rightarrow (P \to R) \):**
   This conditional statement is only false when the antecedent is true and the contradiction is false.

5. **Final Step:**  
   If the statement \( (P \to Q) \wedge (Q \to R) \to (P \to R) \) is true for all possible combinations of the truth values of \( P \), \( Q \), and \( R \), then the theorem is verified.

**The Trace**:
\[
\begin{cases}
P \rightarrow Q \text{ is false when } P = \text{T} \text{ and } Q = \text{F} \\
Q \implies R \text{ is false when } Q = \text{T} \text{ and } R = \text{F} \\
P \rightarrow R \text{ is false when } P = \text{T} \text{ and } R = \text{F}
\end{{cases}
\]

**Final Trace**:
\[
\begin{cases}
(P \rightarrow Q) \text{ is false when } P = \text{T} \text{ and } Q = \text{F} \\
(Q \rightarrow R) \text{ is false when } Q = \text{T} \text{ and } R = \text{F} \\
(P \rightarrow R) \text{ is false when } P = \text T \text{ and } R = \text{F}
\end{cases}
\]

**Final Answer**:  
The correct trace is:
\[
\begin{align}
\boxed{
\begin{cases}
P & Q & R & P \to Q & Q \to R & P \to R & (P \to Q) \wedge (Q \to R) & (P \to Q) \wedge (Q \to R) \to (P \to R) \\
\text{T} & \text{T} & \text{T} & \text{T} & \text{T} & \text{T} & \text{T} & \text{T} \\
