2. Influence on Galaxy Formation:

- Galaxy formation is crucial because black holes, such as supermassive black holes (SMBHs) at the centers of galaxies, are believed to form in relation to their galaxies.  
- Dark matter halos play a vital role in the distribution and distribution of baryonic matter, influencing the distribution of stars and the overall distribution of matter in galaxies. This, in turn, affects the formation of stars and the formation of the surrounding matter that can eventually accreton a black hole.

