- \( W = \text{work done} \)
- \( n = \text{number of moles} \)
- \( R = 8.314 \text{ J/mol·K} = 0.0821 \text{ L·atm/mol·K} \) (using L-atm as the pressure and volume units)
- \( T = \text{temperature} \)
- \( V_1 = \text{initial volume} \)
- \( V_2 = \text{final volume} \)

First, we need to find the temperature \( T \). We can use the ideal gas law:

\[
PV = nRT
\]

Substitute the initial conditions:
\[
(2 \text{ atm})(4 \text{ L}) = (2 \text{ mol})(0.0821 \text{ L·atm/mol·K}) T
\]
\[
